---
metadata:
  layer: root
  profile: root
  scope: ./
  version: "1.0"
  description: Rust norm-spec repository governance

template:
  required_files: [AGENTS.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, ROADMAP.md, Cargo.toml]
  required_directories: [crates/, docs/, schema/, templates/, tests/]
  naming_convention:
    - "kebab-case for crate and planning directory names"
    - "UPPERCASE.md for stable top-level reference documents"
  single_source_of_truth:
    - source: docs/SPEC.md
      for: the .norm format
    - source: docs/decisions.md
      for: architectural and product rationale
    - source: docs/planning/status.md
      for: current development state

agent_rules:
  update_order:
    - "Record scope-changing decisions before implementation"
    - "Update the behavior contract with parser or validator changes"
    - "Run Rust quality gates before merge"
  reference_policy:
    target_must_exist: true
    allow_external: false
    require_description: true

strong_references:
  - type: source
    target: /docs/SPEC.md
    sync: auto_pull
    validation: strict
    description: The prose specification defines the format implemented here
---

# Repository conventions

Keep the format, schemas, behavior contract, and implementation aligned. The
Rust engine is consumer-independent; pi-specific behavior belongs downstream.
